+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool input against the registered JSON Schema `inputSchema` before invoking the tool executor, returning a structured `ToolResponse` on rejection rather than throwing so the AI model can inspect the failure and retry within the tool loop.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on schema violation (`required`, `type`, or `enum`), it returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failing property path and constraint without invoking the executor or leaking offending values in the response or logs, while still throwing `Unknown tool: <name>` for unregistered tool names ([validated by: rejects schema-violating input with a ToolResponse without invoking the executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L23)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared JSON Schema types, and `enum` without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, applying `default` values, or coercing types, forwarding valid input with unlisted properties to the executor unchanged ([validated by: forwards valid input with extra properties unchanged without defaults or type coercion](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L75)).
+- A static tool definition compiles its `inputSchema` once at `register` time and throws an error naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled, whereas a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves and validates against the schema current on each `execute` call ([validated by: compiles static schemas once at registration and resolves dynamic schemas per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L97)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a schema validation rejection inside `chatOrchestrator`, the rejection `result` is sent back to the AI provider as a `tool_result` so the model can correct its call on the next tool round ([validated by: feeds schema validation rejections back into the orchestrator tool loop for retry](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L162)).
+
+## Logging and diagnostics
+
+- Validation failures are logged with the tool name and failing schema paths or keywords, never with raw input or property values.
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still logs `inputKeys` before validation and `execution complete` only when the executor runs.
